// @run
// @log green
// @log green
// @log 0
// @log c=green
// @log green
// @hint redundant type annotation: `v` is inferred as `"red" | "green"` — remove it to lean on inference
// @hint redundant type annotation: `w` is inferred as `"red" | "green"` — remove it to lean on inference
// @hint redundant type annotation: `deep` is inferred as `"red" | "green"` — remove it to lean on inference
// AN INLINE LITERAL UNION IS A STRING REF AND A LITUNION ARRAY IS AN ATOM LIST, and a module
// GLOBAL annotated with the inline spelling and fed by an element read sits across that seam.
// Its cell is slotted as the atom, so the READ has to widen; `letInitIsLitAtom` declined the
// annotated face and `print` took the plain-i32 arm, printing the interned id. D1541.
//
// THE `redundant type annotation` HINTS ABOVE ARE THE RULE ITSELF, DECLARED RATHER THAN
// SILENCED: the checker agrees about the TYPE, which says nothing about whether the two
// spellings agree about the REP — and here they did not. Removing the annotations makes
// the file green for the wrong reason.
//
// NO `type` DECLARATION MAY BE ADDED TO THIS FILE. An alias whose member set is exactly the
// inline spelling's makes the annotation resolve to the alias's own arena index, both ends
// agree again, and the fixture stops pinning anything (the ablation is on D1541).
const arr: ("red" | "green")[] = ["green"]
const v: "red" | "green" = arr[0]
print(v)
const w: "red" | "green" = v
print(w)
if v == "red" { print(1) } else { print(0) }
print("c=" + v)
const nested: ("red" | "green")[][] = [["green"]]
const deep: "red" | "green" = nested[0][0]
print(deep)
